MaxLineLength:DiagnosticXrActivity.kt$DiagnosticXrActivity.&lt;no name provided&gt;$// S0283 Parallax Stereo-depth wiring (0.0 to 1.0 translates to horizontal shift in GLES uniform) Let's store this in a static/dynamic property. The rendering thread can read it or we set it. We will set this on the renderThread directly.
MaxLineLength:DiagnosticXrActivity.kt$DiagnosticXrActivity.Companion$// S0290 (owner round 3 2026-05-22): full coverage matrix - 3 projections × 3 stereo layouts × {image, video} = 18 entries plus the original FLAT mono (moraine lake). Stereo variants ship with diagnostic L/R overlays (see setup_test_vr.ps1) so the viewer can verify per-eye routing by closing one eye in the headset.
MaxLineLength:DiagnosticXrActivity.kt$DiagnosticXrActivity.Companion$// S0290 Phase 09: onPause runs on the main thread; keep the join wait shorter than the standard ANR window so re-entry is responsive while still giving the render thread time to release EGL/OpenXR resources.
MaxLineLength:DiagnosticXrActivity.kt$DiagnosticXrActivity$/** S0290 Phase 09: synchronously request exit, wait up to [timeoutMs] for the render thread to finish, and null the reference so the next [surfaceCreated] starts a fresh thread. */
MaxLineLength:DiagnosticXrActivity.kt$DiagnosticXrActivity$/** S0295 Phase 02 step 02.3: when the launch URI is a `content://` resource (the only realistic shape coming from the badge / overflow callers because they hand us a `MediaStore`-backed URI), drain it through `contentResolver.openInputStream` into a cache file the existing decode path can open as a [File]. Returns null on any IO error so the caller can surface a typed `Unavailable(InvalidUri)`. */
MaxLineLength:DiagnosticXrActivity.kt$DiagnosticXrActivity$// onPause normally already tore everything down (Phase 09); this is the belt-and-braces path for the rare process-death-after-pause case where onPause did not get to finish. Same ordering rule: ExoPlayer release before native shutdown.
MaxLineLength:DiagnosticXrActivity.kt$DiagnosticXrActivity$// S0290 Phase 09 + owner round 3 (2026-05-22): order matters. Release ExoPlayer FIRST so it lets go of the Surface it received from runtime.getVideoSurface(); only then tear down the native side which destroys the underlying SurfaceTexture / GL texture. The reverse order caused VideoFrameReleaseHelper to call Surface.setFrameRate on an already-released Surface (logcat: "Surface has already been released") and MediaCodec.flush on a Released codec at every immersive exit.
MaxLineLength:DiagnosticXrActivity.kt$DiagnosticXrActivity$// S0295 Phase 02 step 02.4: render-thread exit from an OpenXR session that ran to its end (user dismissed via input handler after viewing) is the natural "completed" path. CancelledByUser remains the result for the explicit back-press shortcut in onBackPressedDispatcher above.
