MaxLineLength:SmbConnectionManager.kt$SmbConnectionManager$/** Execute block with a pooled SMB connection. Handles connection pooling, retry logic, and health tracking. S0195: trigger network lifecycle bootstrap on first SMB use. */
MaxLineLength:SmbConnectionManager.kt$SmbConnectionManager$/** Get connection for ExoPlayer (synchronous blocking call). Used by SmbDataSource which runs in ExoPlayer's thread pool. Attempts to reuse pooled connection, creates new if needed. IMPORTANT: Caller must NOT close the returned objects - they are managed by the pool. ExoPlayer should only use the DiskShare for file operations. */
MaxLineLength:SmbConnectionManager.kt$SmbConnectionManager$/** Get or create fast-tier SMB client (transaction timeout = 5 s). Used for connections where speed test confirmed &gt; 100 Mbps. */
MaxLineLength:SmbConnectionManager.kt$SmbConnectionManager$/** Get or create slow/degraded-tier SMB client (transaction timeout = 20 s). Default when no speed test data exists or runtime degradation detected. */
MaxLineLength:SmbConnectionManager.kt$SmbConnectionManager$/** Handle network reconnection (e.g., WiFi reconnect with new IP). Invalidates all pooled connections as they may be broken. */
MaxLineLength:SmbConnectionManager.kt$SmbConnectionManager$/** Invalidate and close the pooled ExoPlayer connection for [connectionInfo]. Call this from SmbDataSource.open when a share operation fails with a transport error on a connection that previously passed isConnectionValid() - SMBJ's isConnected flag does not detect TCP-level silent drops until an actual write attempt is made. */
MaxLineLength:SmbConnectionManager.kt$SmbConnectionManager$/** Remove connection from pool and close it synchronously (cascade: share → session → connection). Delegated to [SmbConnectionPool] which owns the lifecycle. */
MaxLineLength:SmbConnectionManager.kt$SmbConnectionManager$/** Reset all SMB connections and clear error state. Public API for manual recovery from connection issues. Closes all connections, resets clients, and clears timeout counters. */
MaxLineLength:SmbConnectionManager.kt$SmbConnectionManager$/** S0061 Phase 02: Purge all pool entries for [host]:[port] AND reset the SMBJ client so its internal Connection cache is also discarded. Called when a transport-level error (Broken pipe, Connection reset) is detected on any operation path. Forces the next [client.connect()] to open a real new TCP socket instead of reusing the stale one that SMBJ keeps in its connection table. Safe to call concurrently - pool operations are atomic; client nullification is done under [resetClients] which is synchronised on `this`. */
MaxLineLength:SmbConnectionManager.kt$SmbConnectionManager$/** S0061 Phase 04: Release SCANNER + PLAYER connections when the app moves to background. BACKGROUND_WORKER connections are preserved so in-flight WorkManager transfers can continue. Called by [SmbBackgroundLifecycleManager] via the lifecycle observer. */
MaxLineLength:SmbConnectionManager.kt$SmbConnectionManager$/** Select SMBJ client for [server]:[port] based on two signals: 1. Runtime health: if [ConnectionThrottleManager] reports degradation, use max-patience client. 2. Speed test data: pick tier (FAST / MEDIUM / SLOW) from last measured read speed. This means a WiFi7 user gets a 5 s QUERY_DIRECTORY timeout (unresponsive = broken immediately), while a user on a slow 4G bridge gets 20 s of patience. */
MaxLineLength:SmbConnectionManager.kt$SmbConnectionManager$/** Set callback for auto-reset notifications. Should be called from Application or ViewModel to show user feedback. */
